From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Age of Decomp patch queue <aod-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:56:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aod: compiler workflow: build the game on Linux x86-64

compiler/backend.py build now accepts Linux x86-64. There the bundle carries the sources, the shader translator
(translator/totk_xlate) and optionally its own Python (python/bin/python3, else the interpreter running the backend);
clang, lld, Ninja and the SDL3, Opus, libvpx, zstd, Vulkan and zlib development files are the system's, as in
tools/linux/build.sh. Before any work the backend checks the tools and links one probe per library, and the versions
of clang, lld and Ninja become the toolchain stamp, so another compiler rebuilds the objects. The workspace lock uses
flock on Linux. tools/hwaoi.py build names hwaoi instead of hwaoi.exe there and passes --toolchain/--deps only when
given. The compiler workflow and lock tests run on Linux too.
